## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_sheets.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Sheets generates a layered-noise pattern that looks like sheets. It can serve as a mask or building block for detailed textures, such as misshapen sheet metal.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Sheets produit un motif de feuilles superposées par bruits, utilisable en masque ou pour une tôle déformée.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude scales values before Center; Center offsets them; Mask Contrast adjusts contrast", "Pattern: Element Size, Offset, Tile Size", "Primary Distortion: horizontal distortion along Y, roughening the edges", "Primary Roughness: sharper detail on the base layer", "Secondary Mask: visibility and spread of the highlights", "Secondary Amount: how many highlights appear", "Secondary Distortion: vertical distortion along X on the highlight layer", "Seed: randomizes the output while keeping the same look", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Layers can hold negative values and values above 1; use Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum", "Complement (1 - x) works as expected only for values from 0 to 1", "Fold has no visible effect when all values are positive", "Tile Size should match the aspect ratio of non-square images", "Post-processing Contrast differs from Noise Contrast on some noise nodes"]

